From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol drops an obstacle
 it found no edge for

ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol, on reaching an obstacle face, sets c1obstacle and replaces HC with a
fresh BRepAdaptor_Curve2d, then looks for the arc edge among the obstacle face's edges and
initialises HC with it:

  c1obstacle = true;
  ...
  HC = new BRepAdaptor_Curve2d();
  ... find newedge among Fv's edges by IsSame(anArcEdge) ...
  if (!newedge.IsNull()) { HC->Initialize(newedge, Fv); ... return true; }
  else { prepareDefaultReturn(); return false; }

When no edge matches, the else branch returns false and leaves HC as the default-constructed
adaptor, which holds no curve, with c1obstacle still true.

The caller, ChFi3d_Builder::PerformSetOfSurfOnElSpine, tests "not Ok and HC null" to detect the
end of the chain:

  if ((!Ok1 && HC1.IsNull()) || (!Ok2 && HC2.IsNull())) { ... BuildPlane or throw ... }

An empty but non-null HC passes that test, and obstacleon1/obstacleon2, which receive c1obstacle,
then select the obstacle path, which hands HC to ChFi3d_FilBuilder::PerformSurf. The SurfRst walk
evaluates it through Adaptor3d_CurveOnSurface::EvalD1, and Geom2dAdaptor_Curve::D1 falls to its
default arm and dereferences a null curve: a SIGSEGV that no catch (...) in a bridge can reach,
since OCC_CATCH_SIGNALS is inert in this build.

Setting HC null and c1obstacle false in that branch gives the caller the state it already handles
for "no obstacle". The sibling failure in the same block, returning false when HSref or HCref is
null, leaves HC null, which the caller does handle, and is left alone.

Found by instrumenting the pinned kernel with override-linked copies of BRepAdaptor_Curve2d.cxx,
Adaptor3d_CurveOnSurface.cxx and ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx (Scripts/repro/occt1568-fillet-opposite-edge/):
the one Adaptor3d_CurveOnSurface::EvalD1 call before the fault dereferences a default-constructed
BRepAdaptor_Curve2d that is never initialised, and the branch above fires exactly twice at the
crashing radius and never at 1.49 or 1.5000001. BRepAdaptor_Curve2d::Initialize leaving an adaptor
empty for an edge with no pcurve was the first hypothesis and is ruled out: it never fires on this
model. BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet on the reporter's model from OCCT#1568, one edge at a time, 42
edges and nine radii (378 cases): the eight edges that crashed at radius 1.5 now report
IsDone() == false, as 1.4999999 does, and the other 370 cases are unchanged.

Reported upstream as OCCT#1568. Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#2881.

diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
index 9a6c5801a..77728aa97 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/ChFi3d/ChFi3d_Builder_2.cxx
@@ -1557,6 +1557,9 @@ bool ChFi3d_Builder::StartSol(
         }
         else
         {
+          // The obstacle face has no edge to follow, so HC holds no curve: this is not an obstacle.
+          HC.Nullify();
+          c1obstacle = false;
           prepareDefaultReturn();
           return false;
         }
